If the index bounces, the 23,000 to 23,050 zone is the first hurdle. This is the broken support, so selling pressure can show up again there. On the downside, 22,500 is the first level to watch. A break below it can pull the Nifty down to the April low of 22,182.
 Strategy : Sell Nifty Futures at CMP or on bounce towards 23,000, with a stop-loss of 23,200 on a closing basis, and target of 22,500 – 22,182.
